The Termux OpenSL namespace wrapper populates its exported IID pointers lazily
when the first wrapped function is called. Defer Oboe's IID lookup until after
slCreateEngine so the wrapper has initialized them. Native system-library
behavior is unchanged because none of the IIDs are used before this point.

--- a/src/opensles/EngineOpenSLES.cpp
+++ b/src/opensles/EngineOpenSLES.cpp
@@ -78,25 +78,6 @@ bool EngineOpenSLES::linkOpenSLES() {
